# A separate checkout that sits alongside this one. Git cannot track the
# contents of a nested repository - it stores only a commit reference, so a
# clone of this repo would get an empty directory and a warning instead of the
# code - and plain `git add -A` adds it as a gitlink on every commit otherwise.
